{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/44976-converting-a-sublimati","id":44976,"title":"\"Converting\" a Sublimati","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-08T10:29:38-08:00","id":44976,"title":"\"Converting\" a Sublimati","content":"In my current campaign the players are keeping and feeding a sublimati in their house. They're convinced she's a promethean, only a bit wrong... In any case, they want to make her whole which definitely is major milestone material. If they succeed she'll start as a humanity 0 promethean with centimani as the base refinement instead of stannum. The question is how to &quot;convert&quot; her. <br /> I've told them redoing the generative act would probably just make new pandorans or at best making a wholly new individual.<br /> Frankly I'm at a loss myself, does anyone here have an idea of how to turn this into some sort of quest/plot, specifically how to give a sublimati its own Azoth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1944-cobalus","name":"cobalus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T17:34:47-08:00","id":45244,"title":"","content":"The first two ideas that come to mind for me are 1) Qashmal intervention, and 2) a powerful &amp; rare Pandoran Transmutation. So then the Throng either has to figure out how to summon a Qashmal and get it to do what they want, or ingratiate themselves with a powerful Centimanus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T18:45:11-08:00","id":45282,"title":"","content":"it's been a long time since I read it but I remember something about after they have fed on a promethean they absorb other sublimati and pandorans and have a chance to form a promethean if everything lines up just right","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T22:15:48-08:00","id":45394,"title":"","content":"You need to give the Sublimatus some Azoth, so you need a source of Azoth. Four possibilities off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> 1. A <i>qashmal</i> sacrifices itself and merges with the Sublimatus. <br /> 2. A Firestorm infuses the Sublimatus with Pyros, and enough Azoth distills out of it to form a dot of Azoth. <br /> 3. Someone performs the generative act on the Sublimatus, as if it was a corpse. <br /> 4. A mad scientist extracts a dot of Azoth from a Promethean and inserts it into the Sublimatus. <br /> <br /> All require Storyteller fiat; but they\u2019re also more or less consistent with <b>Promethean</b> metaphysics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T22:55:10-08:00","id":45401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/44976-converting-a-sublimati?p=45282#post45282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's been a long time since I read it but I remember something about after they have fed on a promethean they absorb other sublimati and pandorans and have a chance to form a promethean if everything lines up just right</div> </div> </div> </div>You're thinking of Praecipitati, which are big temporary mergers of Pandoras formed around a core Pandoran \u2014 who has had a full Pyros pool for some number of days, triggering a feeding frenzy whereby they incorporate other Pandorans into a larger cluster for about a scene \u2014 which may, upon the collapse of the cluster, result in the Pandoran spontaneously becoming a Sublimatus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T03:25:46-08:00","id":45478,"title":"","content":"I'll be planting the idea that they can offer the sublimatis creator to her but they're big on moral behaviour so that's probably out. I was also considering the God-Machine in &quot;These mortal engines&quot;. But one of the players have decided that Pyrrha (named the sublimati that) is their sister and that its their business to &quot;fix&quot; her, he has studied Occultism a lot even though its outside the characters normal purview. It'd be a bit of a copout if a Lilithim just gave her Azoth.<br /> If I say made it a extended Occult roll, what should I aim for? Would you say the Aqua Vitae from the Water of Life could help?<br /> Otherwise, a combined medicine/occult extended for a Azoth furnace-transplant?<br /> I was also thinking about External Alchemy in Second Sight, the players crafting potions of distilled pyros and with training (and probably some help) one of the players would be gifted a piece of the divine fire to finish his work.<br /> In any case some sort of mad obsession should take place, the player endlessly toiling away in a makeshift lab with the sole goal of making her broken sister whole.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the ideas, kickstarted my brain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1944-cobalus","name":"cobalus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T14:06:06-08:00","id":48460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cobalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/44976-converting-a-sublimati?p=45478#post45478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be planting the idea that they can offer the sublimatis creator to her but they're big on moral behaviour so that's probably out. I was also considering the God-Machine in &quot;These mortal engines&quot;. But one of the players have decided that Pyrrha (named the sublimati that) is their sister and that its their business to &quot;fix&quot; her, he has studied Occultism a lot even though its outside the characters normal purview. It'd be a bit of a copout if a Lilithim just gave her Azoth.<br /> If I say made it a extended Occult roll, what should I aim for? Would you say the Aqua Vitae from the Water of Life could help?<br /> Otherwise, a combined medicine/occult extended for a Azoth furnace-transplant?<br /> I was also thinking about External Alchemy in Second Sight, the players crafting potions of distilled pyros and with training (and probably some help) one of the players would be gifted a piece of the divine fire to finish his work.<br /> In any case some sort of mad obsession should take place, the player endlessly toiling away in a makeshift lab with the sole goal of making her broken sister whole.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the ideas, kickstarted my brain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Instead of making it a series of rolls, i would much rather make it a pilgrimage onto itself. Consider the following;<br /> <br /> Prometheans are human-looking, but monsters by human standarts. A Sublimatus is Promethean-looking, but a monster by Promethean standarts. In that sense, would it be so very far off to conclude that a truely dedicated Sublimatus can trancend their monstrous nature, and become slightly less monstrous, by becoming a Promethean? A Proto-New Dawn?<br /> It could allow the characters a chance to reflect on how much they they have learned, as they try to teach Pyrrha all the lessons they have accrued while also serving as a grim reminder of how much they stand to loose if they forsake their humanity, but alittle.<br /> It would also show them how important humanity is, no matter what the out come. If they succeed, they have showed that even a horrid abomination such as a sublimatus has the capacity for self improvement, and then so would they. If they fail, they'll see the Pyrrha for the monster she, and realise that what they thought was their friend only weeks ago, have now become their enemy. An important lesson regarding the fragility of relationships.<br /> Alternately, the outcome could be a mixture of both. They could succeed in showing her the value of humanity, while she succeeds in showing them that even good people can be monstrous sometimes. That the world isn't black and white, and that you cant differenciate in whats a &quot;Monsters&quot; and whats a &quot;Person/Human&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course this idea is much more contered in the philosophical theme of Promethean, rather than the Alchemical one, you mentioned. Both are bloody awesome, and a central part of Promethean. I just find the philosophy to suit my fancy alittle better.<br /> <br /> Honestly, i'm abselutely in love with the idea, no matter if you end up going with Alchemy or philosophy! Please keep us posted on how it progresses.<br /> <br /> Cheers, and best of luck.<br /> ~ Krobeles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T16:57:43-08:00","id":49353,"title":"","content":"Thanks, she is actually very integral to the plot. The players treat her like a throngmate and spends time teaching her how to read and basic ethics among other things. She makes the players think about what makes one human, our best roleplaying is usually with Pyrrha. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> She's a bit like a cat, strong-minded and stays around because the players feed her. <br /> Anyway, the topic is mainly about how I'd explain her change but maybe I should just let it be a, as you say, proto-new dawn. I'm considering kidnapping her or forcing the players to choose between her and another Promethean.<br /> (Typing on a pad so writing long sentences is a huge hassle...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1944-cobalus","name":"cobalus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T08:32:29-07:00","id":1406277,"title":"","content":"Mayhaps you could do something like a combination of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a>'s 'ingratiating selves with a centimanus' idea, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>'s 2nd, 3rd and 4th ideas and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1958_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1958\" data-vbnamecard=\"1958\">Krobeles</a>' idea together with this idea linking them together; a Centimanus, centuries ago somehow managed to figure out some sort of alchemical ritual-surgery-equation that, if done right, allows the transformation of a Sublimatus into a Promethean of your specifications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T10:30:00-07:00","id":1406293,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Try not revive threads over a year old.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}